  "nl_text": "This database schema is called rschema_0071 and it has three tables: mine, safety_officer, and safety_inspection_record. The mine table has five columns: mine_number, mine_name, mine_location, person_in_charge, and a primary key constraint on mine_number. The safety_officer table has six columns: safety_officer_number, name, gender, telephone, position, and mine_number, with a primary key constraint on safety_officer_number and a foreign key constraint on mine_number that references the mine table. The safety_inspection_record table has four columns: inspection_date, inspection_content, inspection_results, and inspector, with a primary key constraint on mine_number and inspection_date and a foreign key constraint on mine_number that references the mine table.",
  "gold_question": "Business requirement description: A non-metallic mining company has multiple mines, and each mine has multiple safety officers. The safety officer has information such as safety officer number, name, gender, telephone number, and position. The mine has information such as mine number, name, location, and person in charge. During each safety inspection, it is necessary to record the inspection date, inspection content, inspection results, and inspector information. The information system needs to be able to perform statistical analysis on the safety inspection situation of the mine.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0071.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0071\nCREATE TABLE `mine` (\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mine_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mine_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`mine_number`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `safety_officer` (\n  `safety_officer_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `telephone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`safety_officer_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `safety_officer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`mine_number`) REFERENCES `mine` (`mine_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `safety_inspection_record` (\n  `inspection_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_results` text NOT NULL,\n  `inspector` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`mine_number`, `inspection_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `safety_inspection_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`mine_number`) REFERENCES `mine` (`mine_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
